    },
    {
      "block_id": "page-0215-block-0041",
      "order": 41,
      "text": "■\n■Supported by three RCTs.68,69 Associated with QTc prolongation. Rarely used\n",
      "bbox": [
        171.88909912109375,
        428.5019226074219,
        422.3113098144531,
        437.20941162109375
      ],
      "text_sha256": "cf0858dcda6549f2f82e0dbf3ef83e60b171cdb404406d4588794178fef33b67"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "page-0215-block-0042",
      "order": 42,
      "text": "Notes\n",
      "bbox": [
        61.891204833984375,
        457.32440185546875,
        82.30620574951172,
        466.2119140625
      ],
      "text_sha256": "38732073f309589131fec63f417896537e63d27fc29fcf7c60d5f47379f0887a"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "page-0215-block-0043",
      "order": 43,
      "text": "■\n■Always consider the use of mood stabilisers and/or antidepressants, especially where mood disturbance is \n",
      "bbox": [
        61.888999938964844,
        467.5019226074219,
        409.0116882324219,
        476.20941162109375
      ],
      "text_sha256": "45e6b4d1843446228eeff69f289691cfa02517aeab239a7104105fa607cb6d88"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "page-0215-block-0044",
      "order": 44,
      "text": "thought to contribute to symptoms70–72\n",
      "bbox": [
        70.88909912109375,
        477.4994201660156,
        195.73358154296875,
        486.2069091796875
      ],
      "text_sha256": "75555098d05ddcb2a79fe8c7ac7de0e19f0bbbdccebe669d27a6264969819eb5"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "page-0215-block-0045",
      "order": 45,
      "text": "■\n■Other options include adding pimozide, olanzapine or sertindole. None is recommended: pimozide and \n",
      "bbox": [
        61.888999938964844,
        487.3218994140625,
        413.7591247558594,
        496.20941162109375
      ],
      "text_sha256": "5c56074a39a9291eb1f60c5c8e8d849845b65a6d4bc676484be3dc0db05bb88e"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "page-0215-block-0046",
      "order": 46,
      "text": "sertindole have important cardiac toxicity, and the addition of olanzapine is poorly supported73 and likely to \nexacerbate metabolic adverse effects. Studies of pimozide74,75 and sertindole76 have shown no effect. One small \nRCT supports the use of ginkgo biloba,77 another two support the use of memantine.78,79 Another study \nsuggests possible benefit of augmentation with acetyl-L-carnitine,80 and a case study reports good outcome \nwith thyroxine.81 A single RCT describes successful use of sodium benzoate.82 Minocycline is probably not \neffective.63,83 Glycine may be effective for positive symptoms, but studies are of poor quality.84 A small case series \n(n = 6) found benefit to adding pimavanserin.85\n",
      "bbox": [
        70.88618469238281,
        497.4994201660156,
        434.7627868652344,
        566.2069091796875
      ],
      "text_sha256": "4481f506102d2874113d9f1f7abb9f38aac276c66ce452951e060c6fadf3d4c1"
    }
  ],
